  "comment": "Answers to 'How did you hear about us?'. 'id' is what the profile stores (TailorIT's referral source, canonicalized). 'display' is the name shown and typed after 'Other'. 'names' are primary surfaces (an exact match), 'aliases' curated ones (0.97); a source whose usual wording should match only as an alias, such as 'Employee referral', has no names. 'mentions' are the phrases the mention rule finds inside a longer option ('Job Board - LinkedIn'): brand names only, never generic words such as 'job board', which would make every such option mention a second source. 'Someone who works here told me' is deliberately absent: the golden table's P59 leaves it to the LLM tiebreak. 'parents' are the kinds of source a source is one of (Indeed is a job board, LinkedIn a job board and social media): an option naming one is the same answer, less precisely, so it is never a hard conflict for the source.",
